  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "testlesson-review-next-steps-e6825c60-c0a3-43e5-b6be-2cb8f13be07a",
        "text": "Remember the awesome owl webpage we built? We used HTML to structure its content, like adding headings, paragraphs, and images!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/b04ca34e62980d1b7b1b698fd4bc552d-testlesson-review-next-steps-panel-1-8d253672-7dc6-49bc-95cc-a0c41646ac87.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-review-next-steps-9fe70d30-af76-4e11-9991-e129816783ad",
        "text": "Then, we used CSS to make our owl webpage look great! Colors, fonts, and layout – all styled with CSS to bring it to life.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/71dc446bed48f18fd6de66163e9daf86-testlesson-review-next-steps-panel-2-00e0033b-f363-430a-8070-030cbe598ae0.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-review-next-steps-ef22cac2-7948-4165-a7a1-3f161a2cba55",
        "text": "HTML gives content structure, and CSS makes it beautiful. They work hand-in-hand to create amazing websites, just like a team!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/4c7649b0869ef3dfa570119c0908f5e6-testlesson-review-next-steps-panel-3-cc8c1d50-778a-48b4-b529-866c8697576f.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-review-next-steps-4c056406-b93f-4189-be15-720f037a62fd",
        "text": "Now, let's get creative! What if you added more text, new paragraphs, or even a list of cool owl facts to your webpage using HTML?",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/932d62262e0729ae8df7422680eb9113-testlesson-review-next-steps-panel-4-7324b724-46d8-4ccd-b580-c245d2f35c8b.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-review-next-steps-241f54dd-675e-49f4-a5cd-7746e75390d9",
        "text": "You can also explore different CSS styles! Try changing background colors, using new fonts, or rearranging elements to give your page a unique look.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/174b454438b26896693d5d6dfdfec453-testlesson-review-next-steps-panel-5-c6ad9104-578a-489d-b410-198d10d40957.png",
        "layout": "text-top-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-review-next-steps-09586886-9f90-4e1d-a84e-0209d24e2771",
        "text": "The web is your canvas! Experiment, explore, and make your owl webpage uniquely yours. You've got this – keep coding!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/3bc4e4b35908a968dc33aca76ea4ec5e-testlesson-review-next-steps-panel-6-f0f4a251-6e54-4df5-a389-7807607f8ae0.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      }
    ],
    "generate_prompt": "Summarize the key HTML and CSS concepts learned in building the owl webpage. Encourage students to explore adding more content, images, or different styles on their own."
  },
